{"strongs": "H7896", "word": "שִׁית", "translit": "shit", "root": "שית", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "put, set", "definition": "שִׁית verb put, set ( Nö Beitr. z. Semitic Sprachwiss, 39 f. ; compare Phoenician שת Lzb 375 ; Ecclus שית Passive participle Eccl 31:27 (?); see also ( Nö l.c. 41 ) Syriac quality, appearance ); — Qal Perfect 3 masculine singular שָׁת Gen 4:25 +, 3 feminine singular שָׁ֫תָה 1Sam 4:20 +, 2 masculine singular שַׁ֫תָּה Ps 8:7 שַׁ֫תָּ Ps 90:8 , suffix שַׁתַּ֫נִי Ps 88:7 ; Ps 88:9 , 1 singular שַׁ֫תִּי Ps 73:28 +; 3 plural שָׁ֫תוּ Exod 33:4 + 3 t., metaplastic יָשִׁית Ps 49:15 ; Ps 73:9 (other forms not found); Imperfect 3 masculine singular יָשִׁית Exod 21:22 +, jussive יָשֵׁת Job 9:33 , וַיָּ֫שֶׁת Gen 30:40 +; 3 feminine singular suffix וַתְּשִׁתֵ֫חוּ Ruth 4:16 , תְּשִׁיתֵ֫מוֺ Ps 21:10 +, 1 singular suffix אֲשִׁתֶ֫נּוּ 1Kgs 11:34 Imperative masculine singular שִׁית Prov 27:23 , שִׁיתָ֫ה Ps 9:21 ; Ps 141:3 feminine singular שִׁ֫תִי Jer 31:21 , etc.; Infinitive absolute שֹׁת Isa 22:7 construct שִׁית Job 30:1 +; Passive participle וְשִׁית ( Jer 13:16 Qr , but read Kt יָשִׁית ); suffix שִׁתִי Exod 10:1 — 1. put, lay hand upon, עַל , Gen 46:4 ( E ), Gen 48:14 ; Gen 48:17 ( J ), Job 9:33 ; Ps 139:5 with עִם in evil partnership, Exod 23:1 ( E ); put ornaments, עַל person, Exod 33:4 ( J ); compare 1Sam 2:8 ; Isa 15:9 ; Job 22:24 ; Ruth 3:15 lay child into ( ב ) bosom Ruth 4:16 put wisdom, ב location, Job 38:36 , compare Prov 26:24 אָשִׁית עֵצוֺת בְּנַפְשִׁי Ps 13:3 , i.e. take counsel, plan; ׳ סַחְסִי בי Ps 73:28 put things תַּחַת רַגְלָיו Ps 8:7 lay (penalty) עַל person Exod 21:22 ( E ), sin Num 12:11 ( E ), compare (with אֲשֶׁר = where ) Ps 84:4 nearly = give ( נתן ), accusative + ל person Gen 4:25 ( J ; explanation of name שֵׁת ), appoint Ps 9:21 . 2. a. set, station , sheep לְבַדּוֺ Gen 30:40 , compare לֹא שָׁתָם עַל v Gen 30:40 ( J ); accusative of person = appoint ( עַל over ) Gen 41:33 ( E ); set לָמוֺ person ( ל 3 b ) + ב location Ps 73:18 , so (accusative) Ps 88:7 and (object person omitted) Ps 12:6 , set crown לְראֹשׁוֺ Ps 21:4 , set one ( מִן partitive) לְכִסֵּא Ps 132:11 set person among ( ב person) 2Sam 19:29 ; Jer 3:19 , compare ( עִם ) Job 30:1 set watch לְפִי Ps 141:3 , snares לִי Ps 140:6 , enmity, בֵּין person Gen 3:15 ( J ); iniquities לְנֶגְדֶּ֑ךָ Ps 90:8 , compare Ps 101:3 set, direct face, אֶל location Num 24:1 ( J ), eyes לִנְטוֺת בָּאָרָץ Ps 17:11 . \\ \\ b. in phrase לֵב לְ ׳ שׁ set one's mind to , give heed, attention (compare שׂוּם 2 b ), Exod 7:23 ( E ), 2Sam 13:20 ; Jer 31:21 ; Ps 48:14 ; Prov 22:17 ; Prov 27:23 , with אֶל Job 7:17 , absolute 1Sam 4:20 ; Ps 62:11 ; Prov 24:32 I reflected . \\ \\ c. set, fix , נְּבוּל Exod 23:31 ( E ; with מִן ֗֗֗ עַד ), תָּשִׁית לִי חֹק Job 14:13 wouldst fix me a limit, Job 38:11 ( וּפאֹ יָשִׁית בִּגְאוֺן גַּלָּיךָ De and others here shall one fix it [the boundary, חֹק , v Job 38:10 ] = it shall be fixed against, etc.: but explanation very forced: Me Kau ׳ יִשָּׁבֵר ג , Bi Bu ׳ יִשְׁבֹּת ג 3. constitute, make one something, 2 accusative, 1Kgs 11:34 I will make him prince , Isa 5:6 ; Isa 26:1 ; Jer 22:6 ; Ps 21:7 ; Ps 84:7 ; Ps 88:9 ( + למוֺ indirect object), Ps 110:1 ; 2Sam 22:12 || Ps 18:12 תְּשִׁיתֵמוֺ שֶׁ֑כֶם Ps 21:13 = thou wilt make them (all) shoulder , make them turn their back, flee (compare Ps 18:41 ); accusative + ל make something into Jer 2:15 = Jer 50:3 ; Jer 13:16 ; Ps 45:17 ( + ב location); accusative + כ compare make one like Hos 2:5 (|| שִׂים ), Isa 16:3 ; Ps 21:10 ; Ps 83:12 ; Ps 83:14 accusative only, make, prepare , feast Jer 51:39 , compare שָׁת קָצִיר לָח Hos 6:11 (read possibly שִׁית , passive participle), make darkness Ps 104:20 = perform signs, ב location Exod 10:1 ( J ). 4. internally transitive, = take one's stand (compare שִׂים 4 a ) הַפָּרָשִׁים שֹׁת שָׁתוּ הַשָּׁ֑עְרָה Isa 22:7 with ׳ עַליֿ ( against ) Ps 3:7 . — יָשִׁית מִמֶּנִּי Job 10:20 ( Kt ; > Qr Imperative וְשִׁית ) is dubious, יָשִׁית = יָשֵׁת : De direct (attention) away from me , compare Di (ellipsis of יָד , פָּנִים , or לֵב ), Du (sc. יָד ; reads Imperative ); Lag (so Bu ) proposes יִשְׁבֹּת , Siegf ( יָדוֺ ) יָוֵב , ᵐ5 Beer (best) שְׁעֵה ( Job 7:19 ), with יְמֵי חֶלְדִּי ( ᵐ5 Bu Be Du ) for יָמַי יחדל probably rightly. Hoph`al (or Qal passive Ges «GKC:53u»§ 53u ), Imperfect 3 masculine singular יוּשַׁת Exod 21:30 ( E ) if a ransom be imposed עָלָיו , v Exod 21:30 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8650')\">BDB8650</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H7896')\">H7896</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8649')\">BDB8649</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8651')\">BDB8651</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>שִׁית</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>put, set</highlightword> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nö')\">Nö<sup>Beitr. z. Semitic Sprachwiss, 39 f.</sup></lookup>; compare Phoenician <bdbheb>שת</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ldzb')\">Lzb<sup>375</sup></lookup>; Ecclus <bdbheb>שית</bdbheb> Passive participle <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 31:27\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(21,31,27)\">Eccl 31:27</ref> (?); see also (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nö')\">Nö<sup>l.c. 41</sup></lookup>) Syriac <placeholder5520/> <highlight>quality, appearance</highlight>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>שָׁת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 4:25\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(1,4,25)\">Gen 4:25</ref> +, 3 feminine singular <bdbheb>שָׁ֫תָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 4:20\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(9,4,20)\">1Sam 4:20</ref> +, 2 masculine singular <bdbheb>שַׁ֫תָּה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 8:7\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(19,8,7)\">Ps 8:7</ref> <bdbheb>שַׁ֫תָּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 90:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"90\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"90\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=